oup 3 is the G#4 32nds.\n   - A sharp stands before group 4, the A#4 32nds.\n   - A natural and \"p\" stand before group 5. Groups 5–8 are the A4 tremolos.\n   This is bar 19 exactly: E4, then G#4 ×4 and A#4 ×4, then A4, A4. The sharp-then-natural on A settles it.\n3. Last stretch (after the second barline): two groups of four separate notes with staccato dots, then a custos. This is the first half of bar 20, the staccato 16ths G#4 G#4 A4 F#4 | G#4 A4 G#4 F#4. The line ends partway through bar 20, so bar 20 counts.\n\nMismatches: the \"f\" in the first stretch isn't in the edition's bar 18 text. That is a dynamic only, not pitch or rhythm. Note heights in the first stretch are only roughly readable.","right":true,"insights":"The copyist writes each tremolo eighth as a beamed group of 32nds, so a full bar has eight groups. At first glance the four-group opening looks like a whole bar, but it is only half of one. The sharp-then-natural on A in the middle bar (A#4 then A4 in bar 19) pinned the alignment. An edition text that marked half-bar or beat boundaries, or listed the dynamics, would have made the partial bars at each end quicker to confirm."},"ttft_ms":34536,"type":"result","duration_ms":41597,"uuid":"851aae08-f16d-49ef-85b6-2d9b2de99a0b","ttft_stream_ms":1687,"time_to_request_ms":484,"first_content_frame_ms":1687,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":3928,"cacheReadInputTokens":523,"cacheCreationInputTokens":5142,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11980859999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3180,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":5142,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
